From 5e09b74121b0448217ac1f97219b40ea46e30529 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 04:25:42 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 14/34] test: add a P2MR fuzz target

Feed structured and corrupted BIP 360 spends to VerifyScript with
SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR. The witness program, the control block, the leaf script,
the leaf satisfaction and the annex are each either taken from a well-formed
spend of a generated script tree or replaced with fuzz data, so both sides of
every consensus rule are reachable. Fuzzed leaf depths that do not describe a
tree fall back to a balanced shape rather than ending the run, so that most
inputs reach script verification.

Besides the usual agreement between the return value and the script error, the
target asserts that clearing SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR turns any of those inputs back
into an accepted unknown witness program.
